[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3527875093","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112731#issuecomment-3527875093","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112731","id":3527875093,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SRxoV","user":{"login":"groud","id":6093119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTMxMTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6093119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud","html_url":"https://github.com/groud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T13:40:55Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T13:41:43Z","body":"Here are the benchmark results:\r\n```\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tVector2i a;\r\n\t\tuint64_t old_time = OS::get_singleton()->get_ticks_usec();\r\n\t\tVector<Vector2i> points = Geometry2D::bresenham_line(Vector2i(), Vector2i(1000000,5000));\r\n\t\tfor (const Vector2i &v : points) {\r\n\t\t\ta = v; // Do something\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tuint64_t new_time = OS::get_singleton()->get_ticks_usec();\r\n\t\tprint_line(\"Before\", new_time - old_time);\r\n\t}\r\n```\r\nvs\r\n```\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tVector2i a;\r\n\t\tuint64_t old_time = OS::get_singleton()->get_ticks_usec();\r\n\t\tfor (const Vector2i &v : Geometry2D::Bresenham(Vector2i(), Vector2i(1000000,5000))) {\r\n\t\t\ta = v; // Do something\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tuint64_t new_time = OS::get_singleton()->get_ticks_usec();\r\n\t\tprint_line(\"After\", new_time - old_time);\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n```\r\ngets me averaging several runs:\r\n```\r\nBefore ~ 25ms\r\nAfter ~ 10ms\r\n```\r\nSo well, x2.5 faster with the new implementation. \r\nThis is with a single huge line though. As for smaller lines it's harder to quantify anyway, as both functions would be quite fast anyway.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3527875093/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3527882029","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112731#issuecomment-3527882029","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112731","id":3527882029,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SRzUt","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T13:42:37Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T13:42:37Z","body":"That looks like it just optimizes out the loop, I'd use some tool to ensure it actually loops and does anything with the data","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3527882029/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3527906140","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112731#issuecomment-3527906140","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112731","id":3527906140,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SR5Nc","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T13:49:08Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T13:50:42Z","body":"It might be solvable to solve the optimization issue by changing `Vector2i a;` to `volatile`. But I usually declare some function in another header, define it in another cpp file, and call it with the final argument (`v`). Since calls to other compile units are blackboxes, that's often a very cheap way to force the compiler to keep the result. Just make sure LTO is disabled.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3527906140/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3527916125","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112731#issuecomment-3527916125","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112731","id":3527916125,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SR7pd","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T13:50:56Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T13:56:09Z","body":"Can also be verified with checking the output\r\n\r\nThough there are some aspects of this that this simple benchmarks misses, the non-bulk nature of this case isn't really represented in this case (so it would verify the case where just getting the bulk, but for longer code in the iteration it might not be representative, temporal locality etc.), so would be useful to benchmark the specific cases in the engine it is used to get real world data","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3527916125/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3527982765","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112731#issuecomment-3527982765","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112731","id":3527982765,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SSL6t","user":{"login":"groud","id":6093119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTMxMTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6093119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud","html_url":"https://github.com/groud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T14:03:38Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T14:03:38Z","body":"> It might be solvable to solve the optimization issue by changing Vector2i a; to volatile. But I usually declare some function in another header, define it in another cpp file, and call it with the final argument (v). Since calls to other compile units are blackboxes, that's often a very cheap way to force the compiler to keep the result. Just make sure LTO is disabled.\r\n\r\nI mean, for me it's very unlikely it gets optimized out. If it were, there would not be a need to spend 10ms doing nothing. That does not make sense.\r\n\r\nI can try another benchmark, but TBH, I don't really wanna spend a ton of time explaining why allocating a huge vector vs not allocating it makes a difference.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3527982765/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528021502","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112731#issuecomment-3528021502","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112731","id":3528021502,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SSVX-","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T14:13:37Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T14:13:37Z","body":"> I mean, for me it's very unlikely it gets optimized out. If it were, there would not be a need to spend 10ms doing nothing. That does not make sense.\r\n\r\nI noticed that too.\r\nTo be honest, the fact that it _did not_ pass in 0ms is a bit surprising to me. gcc and clang are very good at recognizing when a variable or iterator can be omitted from the build.\r\nDid you run the benchmark in a dev build, or in an optimized build?\r\n\r\n> I can try another benchmark, but TBH, I don't really wanna spend a ton of time explaining why allocating a huge vector vs not allocating it makes a difference.\r\n\r\nI agree, It's obvious that avoiding the allocation should help performance.\r\n\r\nHowever, CPU optimization is not always very straight-forward. Changing something that should obviously be faster can be slower in actuality because of compiler or cpu architecture details. And even if something was optimized, it's possible that there is a bottleneck elsewhere, so the optimization does not have an effect.\r\n\r\nConsidering this complexity, weighing the potential benefit against potential regressions because of the logical change, is why we expect proofs of optimization for performance PRs.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528021502/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528044170","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112731#issuecomment-3528044170","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112731","id":3528044170,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SSa6K","user":{"login":"groud","id":6093119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTMxMTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6093119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud","html_url":"https://github.com/groud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T14:19:08Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T14:20:05Z","body":"Alright, made the benchmarks anyway with this:\r\n```\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tVector2i a;\r\n\t\tuint64_t old_time = OS::get_singleton()->get_ticks_usec();\r\n\t\tVector<Vector2i> points = Geometry2D::bresenham_line(Vector2i(), Vector2i(1000000,5000));\r\n\t\tfor (const Vector2i &v : points) {\r\n\t\t\ta += v; // Do something\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tuint64_t new_time = OS::get_singleton()->get_ticks_usec();\r\n\t\tprint_line(\"Before\", new_time - old_time);\r\n\t\tprint_line(a);\r\n\t}\r\n```\r\nvs\r\n```\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tVector2i a;\r\n\t\tuint64_t old_time = OS::get_singleton()->get_ticks_usec();\r\n\t\tGeometry2D::Bresenham points = Geometry2D::Bresenham(Vector2i(), Vector2i(1000000,5000));\r\n\t\tfor (const Vector2i &v : points) {\r\n\t\t\ta += v; // Do something\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tuint64_t new_time = OS::get_singleton()->get_ticks_usec();\r\n\t\tprint_line(\"After\", new_time - old_time);\r\n\t\tprint_line(a);\r\n\t}\r\n```\r\n\r\nResults:\r\n```\r\nBefore: ~26ms\r\nAfter: ~11ms\r\n```\r\nSo well, similar as before.\r\n\r\n> Did you run the benchmark in a dev build, or in an optimized build?\r\n\r\nI ran them from the editor, with `dev_build=yes\".\r\n\r\n> Considering this complexity, weighing the potential benefit against potential regressions because of the logical change, is why we expect proofs of optimization for performance PRs.\r\n\r\nI mean, I understand that, but it's one of the few things we have actual tests for in `test_geometry_2d.h`. I think we're pretty safe on the regression parts (unless there are some situations not covered by them. Though well, it's a 2 args functions, there are not that many cases to cover I guess)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528044170/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528050086","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112731#issuecomment-3528050086","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112731","id":3528050086,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SScWm","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T14:20:26Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T14:20:26Z","body":"The tests might not cover all edge cases so at least would need a functional validation that the change doesn't affect function in edge cases","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528050086/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528068615","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112731#issuecomment-3528068615","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112731","id":3528068615,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SSg4H","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T14:24:32Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T14:36:10Z","body":"Thanks for running the test again! I think using addition (along with printing `a`) may work to 'trick' the optimizer.\r\n\r\n> I ran them from the editor, with `dev_build=yes\".\r\n\r\nThat means that the optimizer is disabled. We should probably add this to the guidelines, since it's a common mistake to make with benchmarks. \r\nI hate to ask this, but please run the benchmark again with a non-dev build (debug or release; release is preferred).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528068615/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528143486","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112731#issuecomment-3528143486","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112731","id":3528143486,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SSzJ-","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T14:41:46Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T14:42:33Z","body":"I think it'd also be worth looking at if there's other ways the algorithm could be improved, and if there are any edge cases the tests might not handle correctly, and if other options for optimization might be applicable, it might be possible to estimate the number of points for example and reserve a reasonable amount of storage ahead of time etc., it *should* be possible to estimate it mathematically from the precision and step","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528143486/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528189993","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112731#issuecomment-3528189993","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112731","id":3528189993,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SS-gp","user":{"login":"groud","id":6093119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTMxMTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6093119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud","html_url":"https://github.com/groud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T14:52:20Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T14:52:20Z","body":"> I think it'd also be worth looking at if there's other ways the algorithm could be improved, and if there are any edge cases the tests might not handle correctly, and if other options for optimization might be applicable, it might be possible to estimate the number of points for example and reserve a reasonable amount of storage ahead of time etc.\r\n\r\nI mean, at some point you'll have to trust me on that. The [Bresenham algorithm](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bresenham%27s_line_algorithm) is a very simple and straightforward to implement algorithm. There's not a lot of edge-cases besides vertical/horizontal lines and single-point lines. I've tested the algorithm locally with many line drawn (it works flawlessly), and the unit tests pass too. I am positive nothing will be more efficient to improve the algorithm than avoiding an unnecessary allocation here (the algorithm was if fact designed to do no allocation. It's from 1962, when computers had really limited memory available).\r\n\r\nI don't know what to tell you more than that. It's a fix to an implementation I already knew was suboptimal when I implemented it, I've just had the opportunity to fix it today.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528189993/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528204054","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112731#issuecomment-3528204054","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112731","id":3528204054,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7STB8W","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T14:56:01Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T14:58:03Z","body":"Then the benchmarks should show it, including running profiling on the relevant methods affected by this, it's not no work at all but it's not a lot to just confirm this and confirm that the other considerations and potential other performance aspects are not a problem, I get it but I've seen plenty of very obvious optimizations go away when running release builds and encountering the real world","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528204054/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528213521","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112731#issuecomment-3528213521","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112731","id":3528213521,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7STEQR","user":{"login":"groud","id":6093119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTMxMTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6093119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud","html_url":"https://github.com/groud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T15:00:19Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T15:00:19Z","body":"Anyway, reran the benchmark in release. In fact, it's more like a x20 improvement:\r\n```\r\nBefore: ~9ms\r\nAfter: ~0.6ms\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528213521/reactions","total_count":7,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":4,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528231350","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112731#issuecomment-3528231350","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112731","id":3528231350,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7STIm2","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T15:05:48Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T15:05:48Z","body":"That sounds pretty realistic! There's of course still a possibility that some of the implementation was optimized away due to the constants used in your benchmark, but for me this is along the lines of what I would expect from this change. So I think this suffices as a proof of optimization.\r\nThanks again!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528231350/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528285726","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112731#issuecomment-3528285726","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112731","id":3528285726,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7STV4e","user":{"login":"groud","id":6093119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTMxMTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6093119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud","html_url":"https://github.com/groud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T15:13:48Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T15:16:28Z","body":"Note that, for now, the optimization is not exposed to users, as `bresenham_line` still pushes everything to a vector anyway. It should be doable to expose though, as we could expose the Bresenham class as a [custom iterator](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_advanced.html#custom-iterators). It's not a common pattern in the API though.\r\n\r\nI can do it in another PR if we feel the performance improvement is worth.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528285726/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3528779093","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112731#issuecomment-3528779093","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112731","id":3528779093,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SVOVV","user":{"login":"groud","id":6093119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTMxMTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6093119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud","html_url":"https://github.com/groud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.git