eived_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T18:51:18Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T18:51:18Z","body":"See https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105292 which was just merged and might benefit from the same change.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3529234021/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3532059017","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112731#issuecomment-3532059017","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112731","id":3532059017,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ShvGJ","user":{"login":"groud","id":6093119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTMxMTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6093119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud","html_url":"https://github.com/groud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-14T10:28:50Z","updated_at":"2025-11-14T10:28:50Z","body":"I'm having a second thought about the implementation. While I think the `for( : )` syntax is nice, I kind of hate the fact we have to define two classes for it. I am thinking that, maybe, we can get a simpler implementation with only one simpler class. \r\n\r\nMaybe something that would need to be used that way though:\r\n```\r\nfor (Bresenham b = Bresenham(1000,500); b.is_end(); b.next()) { \r\n    Vector2i point = b.value(); \r\n }\r\n```\r\nWhat do you think?\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3532059017/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3532082763","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112731#issuecomment-3532082763","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112731","id":3532082763,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Sh05L","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-14T10:34:04Z","updated_at":"2025-11-14T10:34:16Z","body":"> I'm having a second thought about the implementation. While I think the `for( : )` syntax is nice, I kind of hate the fact we have to define two classes for it. I am thinking that, maybe, we can get a simpler implementation with only one simpler class.\r\n> \r\n> Maybe something that would need to be used that way though:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> for (Bresenham b = Bresenham(1000,500); b.is_end(); b.next()) { \r\n>     Vector2i point = b.value(); \r\n>  }\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> What do you think?\r\n\r\nIf you want to avoid using two classes, I would prefer the following:\r\n\r\n```c++\r\nIterable<BresenhamIterator> bresenham_iter(Vector2i p_from, Vector2i p_to) {\r\n    return Iterable<BresenhamIterator>(BresenhamIterator(p_from, p_to), BresenhamIterator());\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI introduced `Iterable` basically for the purpose of \"I have two iterator instances, and I want to use C++ syntax to iterate across them\". Which would be your use-case here, I think.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3532082763/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3532092522","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112731#issuecomment-3532092522","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112731","id":3532092522,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Sh3Rq","user":{"login":"groud","id":6093119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTMxMTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6093119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud","html_url":"https://github.com/groud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-14T10:36:22Z","updated_at":"2025-11-14T10:36:22Z","body":"> I introduced Iterable basically for the purpose of \"I have two iterator instances, and I want to use C++ syntax to iterate across them\". Which would be your use-case here, I think.\r\n\r\nOooh, I has no clue we had that. Yeah that seems like a good plan, I'll have a look.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3532092522/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3532101516","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112731#issuecomment-3532101516","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112731","id":3532101516,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Sh5eM","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-14T10:38:15Z","updated_at":"2025-11-14T10:38:55Z","body":"Actually, I say that with the expectation of continuing to use the C++ iterator syntax.\r\nC++ iteration syntax is actually really weird that it requires a begin and end. This doesn't make much sense for bresenham, so maybe your proposed solution _would be_ better (fewer wasted variables).\r\nI wanted to look into ways to avoid this problem for some time, but haven't gotten around to it yet.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3532101516/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3532158225","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112731#issuecomment-3532158225","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112731","id":3532158225,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SiHUR","user":{"login":"groud","id":6093119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTMxMTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6093119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud","html_url":"https://github.com/groud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/repos","events_url":"http